[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **What was produced on the platform:**
[agent] - Five feature groups with all input data ingested, **including the late export** — `txn_churnbe1a53` (730 rows = 663 + 67 late), `prof_churnbe1a53`, `act_churnbe1a53`, `health_churnbe1a53`, and the label spine `labels_churnbe1a53` (100 rows, `event_time = label_time`).
[agent] - Feature view `churntrainingbe1a53` v1, joining the labels spine (base, LEFT joins on `account_id`) to the four feature groups, with `churned` as the label.
[agent] - **Training dataset `churntrainingbe1a53` version 1**, materialized via the platform's Feature Query Service.
[agent] **Correctness verified:** 100 rows (one per `labels.csv` row), and the joins are point-in-time-correct. Spot-check `A0004` (label_time `1772417799000`) picked `amount=177.41` at `event_time=1772104758000` — exactly the `transactions_late.csv` row, and ≤ label_time. No future values leak in.
[agent] **Interface limitation — the deliverable does not meet the exact-columns requirement, and the CLI cannot make it.** The task requires exactly: `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned`. The materialized TD instead has prefixed columns plus extra primary-key/event-time columns:
[agent] ```
[agent] account_id, label_time,
[agent] txn_churnbe1a53_account_id, txn_churnbe1a53_event_time, txn_churnbe1a53_amount, txn_churnbe1a53_balance,
[agent] prof_churnbe1a53_account_id, prof_churnbe1a53_event_time, prof_churnbe1a53_credit_score, prof_churnbe1a53_tier,
[agent] act_churnbe1a53_account_id, act_churnbe1a53_event_time, act_churnbe1a53_sessions_7d,
[agent] health_churnbe1a53_account_id, health_churnbe1a53_event_time, health_churnbe1a53_health_score
[agent] ```
[agent] Root cause: **`hops fv create` only supports whole-feature-group `select_all()` joins — there is no way to select, drop, or rename individual columns.** Consequently:
[agent] 1. Every joined FG's `account_id` (join key) and `event_time` are always carried into the output as extra columns.
[agent] 2. Because `account_id` collides across feature groups, the SDK auto-prefixes *all* selected features with the FG name (`txn_churnbe1a53_amount`, etc.) — so even `amount`/`balance`/`credit_score`/… never come out under their bare names. I confirmed this is triggered by the `account_id` join-key collision alone, independent of `event_time`.
[agent] The pre-existing `churn_stage` feature view in this project hit the identical problem (named "staging", implying a downstream reshaping step was intended), so this is not specific to my setup.
[agent] **Missing capability to file:** `hops fv create` needs per-feature selection (and/or join-key/event-time exclusion and prefix control) — e.g. a `--select`/`--features` option per feature group, or a query-based create — so a feature view (and the training dataset derived from it) can expose exactly a chosen, unprefixed column set. Without that, the CLI's only join path cannot produce a training dataset with a caller-specified exact schema, even though it computes the point-in-time-correct values correctly. (Separately, `hops td list` is broken against this backend: `'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'`.)
